{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic","id":1041571,"title":"Angels and Mind Magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-31T16:51:28-08:00","id":1041571,"title":"Angels and Mind Magic","content":"Hey everyone,<br /> <br /> So, I am hosting a campaign with some players that are mostly mortals (one Awakened) and they have stumbled upon a task the God-Machine is working on. They have a friendly mage that has come to the town to investigate the strange events occurring in town and wants to determine the root cause. While there he has taken some of the players under his wing, promising to help them find out the weird things going on in town if they in return help him find information. So, the Mage is an Acanthus and has Mind 2. The foreman that is overseeing the project for the God-Machine is an Angel and the Mage plans to cast Psychic Domination on him since according to Mage Sight he would look Human from my understanding of Angels.<br /> <br /> What would be the end result? In my mind, the spell proves ineffective and the Mage now grows wary of the foreman since things did not work as expected. <br /> <br /> Would the Angel realize that someone has tried to cast a spell on him? My gut says the Angel would not have a clue that any type of Mind shenanigans were performed and would go about their business.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T17:28:59-08:00","id":1041582,"title":"","content":"Apparently if something has a mind, it can be Psychic Dominated. I think there was a ruling on it in a thread in past two months or something. Doesn't matter if it's human, vampire, spirit, ghost, animal, True Sapient AI, or intelligent awakened brick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T17:46:17-08:00","id":1041590,"title":"","content":"Your comment made me dig a little deeper and I think i found something from way back when:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Targeting an Angel, its Numina, rewriting the Pattern of someone claimed, etc, requires equal parts Prime and Spirit. Angels cannot be summoned. You can try to force one to act in a certain way, but angels are inflexible - if carrying out your wishes conflicts with carrying out the God-Machine's wishes, the Angel's programming wins and the spell has no effect.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:blue\">Or, put another way, God has rolled more successes than you on &quot;angel brainwashing&quot;. Also, no creating members of another major template (by making angels Fall!) without Archmastery. Bad mages, go to back of class</span> </div> </div> </div>This was a statement from Dave on the GMC Stop-Gap Rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T22:23:58-08:00","id":1041694,"title":"","content":"You're pretty much both right. As long as something has what could be considered a mind (regardless of how simple or complex) it can be effected by the Mind Arcanum. <i>But</i>, when it comes to angels, the God Machine essentially already has them under a mind controlling affect, and any attempt to take control of an angel effectively causes a Clash of Wills with the God Machine with which is it always assumed to win.<br /> <br /> At least that's how it is with normal mages, Archmages can probably pull it off if they were willing to deal with the consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T22:56:17-08:00","id":1041701,"title":"","content":"So, it would depend on exactly what the mage commanded the angel to do.<br /> <br /> If it's unrelated or inconsequential to the Mission, then the angel just does that. Angels already have that amount of free will, since that's what allows them to Fall. However, they might find their sudden drop in faith... curious, and might investigate further on their on, which could bite back the mage.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if the mage's command was &quot;Stop doing XXX&quot;, where XXX is what the angel is doing as a part of Mission, or &quot;Do YYY&quot;, where YYY directly sabotages the angel's Mission, then the mind control fails. And even in this case, I wouldn't be surprised if angels come with a firewall that alarms them in case of a hacking attempt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T04:40:19-08:00","id":1041762,"title":"","content":"Well, you also have to take into consideration withstand. Psychic domination is withstood by Resolve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T09:06:11-08:00","id":1041861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1041762#post1041762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you also have to take into consideration withstand. Psychic domination is withstood by Resolve.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which in an Angels case is Resistance (as would any other Withstand), so depedning on the Rank of the Angel the Mage might have a real hard time getting past that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T09:35:15-08:00","id":1041874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1041861#post1041861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which in an Angels case is Resistance (as would any other Withstand), so depedning on the Rank of the Angel the Mage might have a real hard time getting past that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ephemeral beings Withstand with Rank.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T09:58:54-08:00","id":1041889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1041874#post1041874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ephemeral beings Withstand with Rank.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, you're right, that's what I get for just going off of someone else's post and not thinking about it enough.<br /> <br /> So yeah, not as bad as I implied earlier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T10:07:53-08:00","id":1041891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1041590#post1041590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">YThis was a statement from Dave on the GMC Stop-Gap Rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>About this comment.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine seems to have put the angel there in a human disguise for a reason, and 'pretending to be human' is part of the God-Machine's wishes. While I admit I don't know what the angel is actually doing there, unless it's something like, 'Watch this 24/7' it seems like you would have a lot of leeway to look into something else. In other words, you can still be ordered to do stuff that doesn't conflict with what the God-Machine wants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T10:13:12-08:00","id":1041894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1041891#post1041891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The God-Machine seems to have put the angel there in a human disguise for a reason, and 'pretending to be human' is part of the God-Machine's wishes. While I admit I don't know what the angel is actually doing there, unless it's something like, 'Watch this 24/7' it seems like you would have a lot of leeway to look into something else. In other words, you can still be ordered to do stuff that doesn't conflict with what the God-Machine wants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Basically, you can't make the Angel do anything that would result in a Fall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T10:57:36-08:00","id":1043038,"title":"","content":"Unless you're running a Mage-centric game and don't consider the GM to be anything too special. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T11:00:37-08:00","id":1043040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1043038#post1043038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you're running a Mage-centric game and don't consider the GM to be anything too special. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Removing / Inflicting other major templates is forbidden below Archmastery, save Time magic fuckery, mage-centric or no. <br /> This has been made explicit by the devs.<br /> <br /> As always, you are free to ignore that in your own games, and as always, discussions hinging on the STs ability to do whatever they want can't really go anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T13:27:46-08:00","id":1043117,"title":"","content":"Yes. I was simply talking about my own game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I generally throw out anything they put into the rules for crossover balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T13:53:55-08:00","id":1043135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1043117#post1043117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. I was simply talking about my own game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>And nobody else was, which begets the question of what you thought this added to the discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I generally throw out anything they put into the rules for crossover balance. </div> </div> </div>That's not even crossover balance, that's basic setting assumptions. &quot;Supernal magic and Abyssal corruption are not responsible for all or even most of the supernatural phenomena in the Chronicles of Darkness&quot; is a basic truth of Mage's cosmological placement, as is &quot;godlike entities are beyond the reach of Travelers' spells to command.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T19:39:07-08:00","id":1043321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1043038#post1043038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you're running a Mage-centric game and don't consider the GM to be anything too special. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds like a great way to have your ass kicked by the fucking GM and the rest of the play group. I'd kick you the fuck out as a player.<br /> <br /> What's the fucking point of participating in a communal storytelling game if you're just going to be an ass about it?<br /> <br /> What a shitty attitude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T20:24:27-08:00","id":1043332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1043321#post1043321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds like a great way to have your ass kicked by the fucking GM and the rest of the play group. I'd kick you the fuck out as a player.<br /> <br /> What's the fucking point of participating in a communal storytelling game if you're just going to be an ass about it?<br /> <br /> What a shitty attitude.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Uh, he is talking about GM as in God Machine, not Game Master. There is nothing &quot;ass&quot; or &quot;shitty attitude&quot; about saying that for purpose of Mage-centric game, you don't consider GodMachine to be anything special.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T20:39:50-08:00","id":1043343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1043321#post1043321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds like a great way to have your ass kicked by the fucking GM and the rest of the play group. I'd kick you the fuck out as a player.<br /> <br /> What's the fucking point of participating in a communal storytelling game if you're just going to be an ass about it?<br /> <br /> What a shitty attitude.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">Woah Arc, that was uncalled for.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T20:48:03-08:00","id":1043348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1043332#post1043332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh, he is talking about GM as in God Machine, not Game Master. There is nothing &quot;ass&quot; or &quot;shitty attitude&quot; about saying that for purpose of Mage-centric game, you don't consider GodMachine to be anything special.</div> </div> </div> </div>There kinda <i>is</i>, given that even outside the context of Demon the God-Machine is a massive occult conspiracy-engine strung through the material world like so much mechanistic cancer-tissue.<br /> <br /> If you don't want to <i>use</i> a godlike being as a godlike being, you're replicating the infamous &quot;I summon Luna to proclaim my superiority to the werewolves!&quot; behavior that's poisoned much of this gameline's perception in the wider fandom of the franchise if you include it anyway and then extend none of the expected anti-tampering protections to beings that are as near to a direct extension of said godlike entity's will and try to present this as a worthwhile line of discussion in a question about how a scenario could be expected to resolve based on the established setting.<br /> <br /> If you show up just to crow about how <i>In-<b>my</b>-game-we-ignore-basic-setting-conceits</i>, that is not a good attitude to bring to the table in any sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T13:42:47-08:00","id":1044155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1043332#post1043332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uh, he is talking about GM as in God Machine, not Game Master. There is nothing &quot;ass&quot; or &quot;shitty attitude&quot; about saying that for purpose of Mage-centric game, you don't consider GodMachine to be anything special.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks WHW. Not sure why a few people got so hostile. I feel that the devs are always tiptoeing around the beloved God Machine too much since the 2.0 reboot. I think it's perfectly valid to bring this up in a thread about Mind and Angels.<br /> <br /> I just think it's silly that you can use Mind of Vampires, Werewolves, Changelings etc..., but for some reason Angels are untouchable. I thought I would share this so that new Mage STs realized that I support their anti-GM rebellion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I feel it's perfectly acceptable and I encourage STs to make their Mage games Mage-centric. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T15:14:43-08:00","id":1044209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1044155#post1044155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks WHW. Not sure why a few people got so hostile. I feel that the devs are always tiptoeing around the beloved God Machine too much since the 2.0 reboot. I think it's perfectly valid to bring this up in a thread about Mind and Angels.<br /> <br /> I just think it's silly that you can use Mind of Vampires, Werewolves, Changelings etc..., but for some reason Angels are untouchable. I thought I would share this so that new Mage STs realized that I support their anti-GM rebellion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The equivalent of using Mind on angels is not using Mind on werewolves or changelings. It's the equivalent of using Spirit to enslave choirs of Lunes, or using Fate to haggle a deal from a Gentry. This is why they're &quot;untouchable&quot;, even before accounting for developer favoritism that we have no evidence of existing, other than complaints about &quot;Why not lemme do this cool thing I thought of?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel it's perfectly acceptable and I encourage STs to make their Mage games Mage-centric.<br /> </div> </div> </div>That we all agree with, but there's a difference between having individual plays and tables being Mage-centric in the sense of giving mages advantageous ruling in the edge cases of crossover, and making entire settings of other games a mere add-on to another game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T20:04:33-08:00","id":1044344,"title":"","content":"Are Angels as powerful as the Gentry? If so, then I stand corrected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T20:11:21-08:00","id":1044345,"title":"","content":"No, but the God-Machine is (and arguably stronger but in ways that aren't quite comparable) and trying to reprogram an angel will force you into a Clash of Wills with the God-Machine directly instead of just the angel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T20:54:39-08:00","id":1044361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1044344#post1044344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Angels as powerful as the Gentry? If so, then I stand corrected.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mission programmed into an angel by the Machine is so defining to its nature that betraying it causes the angel to briefly <i>cease to exist</i> before it hard-reboots itself into a different metaphysical state. For obvious reasons, this is generally only manageable from the inside by an angel making a decision of its own accord based on faulty information, the unexpected variables of foreign supernatural contamination, or the development of an (at the time) stronger principle or attachment than God gave it to its Mission.<br /> <br /> An angel treats the material world as its home dimension for the purposes of determining where it goes in the rare case that it runs out of Essence and hibernates, has a baseline Manifestation Condition that can be created by any other angel of sufficient power, adds dice or subtracts Essence costs from its Numina in the presence of that Condition, often has the Manifestation that allows it to return to that Condition unless it is the weakest sort of angel that exists, and may well possess the ability to assume an inviolate pretense of human (or animal, object, or building) form and immunity to Essence bleed as an innate gift from its master that takes no resources out of its basic ephemeral loadout.<br /> <br /> An angel whose mission is critically endangered may resort to the markedly less subtle modifications it may apply to its powers, of which it always possesses at least one. These adjustments include: making the success of supernatural powers that would affect the angel contingent on a fuel surcharge; substantial global dice-adders and universal penalty-appliers; and just plain &quot;spend Essence to reduce your target's resistance to your powers&quot; effects. The vast majority of these modifiers have more than one effect \u2014 an angel with the Space Incept can effectively declare its powers to manifest from anywhere within its line of sight, while one with the Time Incept can essentially turn any of its powers into hung spells; Economy straight-up lets angels recycle Aether back into Essence as long as a demon isn't holding it.<br /> <br /> An angel can be refueled by the simple act of burning valuables in its name. An angel can be refueled by the simple act of ritual murder. An angel is a process of the Great Wheel That Turns The World, and as long as it adheres to that niche like it's made to do, its purpose is inviolate.<br /> <br /> This is the sort of thing you come to expect when dealing with beings that are empowered by <i>physics </i>\u2014 try as you might, you're not going to roll more successes than God when it comes to determining intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T22:37:56-08:00","id":1044389,"title":"","content":"You know how the book explicitly states that you can never win a Clash of Wills against an Archmage?<br /> The G-M exists in the same cosmological tier they do, at minimum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T22:47:08-08:00","id":1044393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1044389#post1044389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know how the book explicitly states that you can never win a Clash of Wills against an Archmage?<br /> The G-M exists in the same cosmological tier they do, at minimum.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an aside, I love the hilariously twisted idea of the God-Machine being an entity that protects both the Angels and the Unchained in the Ascention War. There's the possibility that Lucifer is another such being, but with very different motives. Very much headcanon from my own ideas about the God-Machine, but I think that's a good example of a reason <b>not</b> to just override the other gamelines in a Mage campaign. A more complicated cosmology makes for more mysteries for Mages to solve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T09:41:44-08:00","id":1044569,"title":"","content":"I think that just leaves open the interesting trick of getting the Angel to do what you want without directly conflicting with its Mission. You're a Mind mage, be the scalpel, not the hammer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8762-waywardpaladin","name":"WaywardPaladin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T09:28:54-08:00","id":1045150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1044155#post1044155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I just think it's silly that you can use Mind of Vampires, Werewolves, Changelings etc..., but for some reason Angels are untouchable.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>See, the problem with this list is that you CAN use Mind to mess with Demons just fine. That is the equivlency you are looking for, not Angels.<br /> <br /> And as others have said, Mind works on Angels, as long as it doesn't go against their Mission.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T13:25:51-08:00","id":1045344,"title":"","content":"You can divert an angel with mind control, but you can't get it to actually abandon or defy its mission. If you want an angel to go off-mission, your best bet is to try convincing it....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T15:44:13-08:00","id":1045438,"title":"","content":"In general, I *like* the idea of angels + the GM being almost completely unknown by mages. In my game (and it looks like in RAW), no major templates have abilities that allow them to see Angels in Twilight. IIRC the ONLY way is with that one Wolf-Blooded trait that allows you to see EVERYTHING in Twilight. Explains why few are aware of the GM or think it's a big deal. &quot;The God-Machine? Is that some sort of minor Paternoster ochema?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1041874#post1041874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ephemeral beings Withstand with Rank.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to throw the thread way off course but...<br /> <br /> So are people seriously saying that you can bind Gaia with a Potency 11 spell? Kind of strains credulity.<br /> <br /> <br /> My houserule is that Supernatural Tolerances are independent Withstand traits (and, as per multiple withstand rules, use the highest &amp; +1 for each additional trait). So you've got a mage with Resistance trait 3, Gnosis 2 and Signs &amp; Wards Potency 4... they Withstand at 4 + 1 + 1 = 6.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T15:56:46-08:00","id":1045443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bonerstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1045438#post1045438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So are people seriously saying that you can bind Gaia with a Potency 11 spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Read the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghost Summons</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spell does not work on ghosts above Rank 5.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goetic Summons</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spell does not work on Goetia above Rank 5.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Invoke Bane</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This spell does not affect spirits above Rank 5.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Command Spirit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This spell has no effect on spirits above Rank 5.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spirit Summons</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spell does not work on spirits above Rank 5.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banishment</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This spell does not work on spirits above Rank 5.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bind Spirit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This spell does not work on spirits above Rank 5.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Annihilate Spirit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Short of archmastery, this spell cannot affect spirits of Rank 6 or higher.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T16:06:46-08:00","id":1045447,"title":"","content":"I can add that Annihilate Spirit (which is the only one that actually can work on Rank 6+) also has Clash of Wills as a requirement. A very nasty Clash of Wills since 6+ spirits should easily have 30+ dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 02-07-2017, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T16:25:22-08:00","id":1045463,"title":"","content":"Speaking of spells, I've noticed that the Death equivalents of Banishment and Bind Spirit, Exorcism and Revenant, does not have the Rank limit. Interesting implications here, since a mage can theoretically exorcise/bind a god of death (and an Astral god, with the Add Mind option), providing he doesn't get annihilated first.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T16:35:17-08:00","id":1045473,"title":"","content":"Don't read too much into that. It's probably an error, not something intended. Different Arcana, different authors. It's also painfully obvious that Death is rewrites directly from 1st ED, and these spells didn't have Rank restrictions there either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 02-07-2017, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T16:47:58-08:00","id":1045488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1045473#post1045473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Don't read too much into that. It's probably an error, not something intended. Different Arcana, different authors. It's also painfully obvious that Death is rewrites directly from 1st ED, and these spells didn't have Rank restrictions there either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's probably that. Still, I find the Arcana governing for termination and binding souls to the living world not having Rank limit intriguing. Of course, any necromancer stupid enough to actually try tackling a god probably deserves whatever's coming to him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T16:59:13-08:00","id":1045498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1045463#post1045463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of spells, I've noticed that the Death equivalents of Banishment and Bind Spirit, Exorcism and Revenant, does not have the Rank limit. Interesting implications here, since a mage can theoretically exorcise/bind a god of death (and an Astral god, with the Add Mind option), providing he doesn't get annihilated first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rank 6+ already <i>doesn't use the Manifestation system</i>, remember. The added notes in the Spirit spells are essentially a courtesy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Every ephemeral and Supernal entity has dots in an Advantage called Rank, which notes how self-aware and powerful the entity is. Rank technically ranges from 1 to 10 dots, but those with more than Rank 5 are overwhelmingly powerful and too alien to the physical world to support themselves with the Conditions that lesser beings use; their presence in a chronicle should come about through critical conjunctions and momentous events. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T17:30:38-08:00","id":1045515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1045498#post1045498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rank 6+ already <i>doesn't use the Manifestation system</i>, remember. The added notes in the Spirit spells are essentially a courtesy.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, I thought that phrase meant &quot;they use special Manifestation Conditions not in this book&quot;, rather than &quot;they don't use Manifestation Conditions at all.&quot; Oh well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T21:58:43-08:00","id":1045611,"title":"","content":"Regardless... withstand 5 for a &quot;Minor God&quot; is a little ridiculous. I understand mages are supposed to be ridiculously unbalanced... but that's some SERIOUS rocket tag right thar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T22:30:20-08:00","id":1045623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bonerstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1045611#post1045611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless... withstand 5 for a &quot;Minor God&quot; is a little ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>The things are rocking consistent base dicepools in the double digits.<br /> <br /> Withstand reduces spells' effective Potency, and the vast majority of spells that specifically mess with ephemeral beings are Duration-primary. Those that aren't are Exorcism analogues, or else relatively constrained stuff like:<br /> <br /> 1. Know Spirit (which gives you less information for higher-Ranked spirits)<br /> 2. Command Spirit (which only lasts for the Duration, Clashes with commands that violate its self-interest, and may be an Act of Hubris if it's not Inured)<br /> 3. Rouse Spirit (which is Potency-intensive even without being Withstood)<br /> 4. Shape Spirit (most of the same problems as Command with the saving grace being that it doubles as a healing spell)<br /> 5. Annihilate Spirit (which explicitly gives a better-than-usual Clash roll to avoid and is a Master level spell targeting a class of being that explicitly applies its Defense to every type of attack if you don't Reach to manifest the effect directly on top of it).<br /> <br /> Withstand 5 is the highest most characters have to deal with from a single source and the relative frequency with which Incarnae are both secluded and accompanied by other spirits means getting to the point where their Withstand rating is the biggest problem you have in casting on them is a trip and a half to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T05:07:28-08:00","id":1045689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1045623#post1045623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The things are rocking consistent base dicepools in the double digits.<br /> <br /> Withstand reduces spells' effective Potency, and the vast majority of spells that specifically mess with ephemeral beings are Duration-primary. Those that aren't are Exorcism analogues, or else relatively constrained stuff like:<br /> <br /> 1. Know Spirit (which gives you less information for higher-Ranked spirits)<br /> 2. Command Spirit (which only lasts for the Duration, Clashes with commands that violate its self-interest, and may be an Act of Hubris if it's not Inured)<br /> 3. Rouse Spirit (which is Potency-intensive even without being Withstood)<br /> 4. Shape Spirit (most of the same problems as Command with the saving grace being that it doubles as a healing spell)<br /> 5. Annihilate Spirit (which explicitly gives a better-than-usual Clash roll to avoid and is a Master level spell targeting a class of being that explicitly applies its Defense to every type of attack if you don't Reach to manifest the effect directly on top of it).<br /> <br /> Withstand 5 is the highest most characters have to deal with from a single source and the relative frequency with which Incarnae are both secluded and accompanied by other spirits means getting to the point where their Withstand rating is the biggest problem you have in casting on them is a trip and a half to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again with those specific spells? Starting Mastigos character with 3 ranks in Space and 2 Gnosis (and, heck 2 ranks in Fate cuz they saucy like that) hears Uratha complaining about a big bad Rank 5 spirit/idigam. Draws a picture of mean old mister spirit as a -2 sympathy Yantra and uses a rote mudra for +4. Base Potency 1 Duration 3 turns.<br /> 1 Free Reach for Sensory range<br /> 1 Free Reach for Advanced Potency<br /> 1 Free Reach for Advanced Duration<br /> 1 Mana Reach for Indefinite Duration<br /> 1 mana for Sympathetic Range (+1 withstand for not knowing its probably well-known sympathetic name.. but Withstand is 4 for a weak connection anyway: Withstand 6 total)<br /> Conditional duration of &quot;Until the heat death of the sun&quot; or &quot;Until 1000 years passes&quot; or &quot;until the Earth is struck by an asteroid&quot; or another infrequent condition that will eventually happen for 2 levels of Duration.<br /> <br /> Let's assume they cast in the Shadow to avoid Gauntlet Withstand (I'd rule it applies if the spell crossed it)<br /> <br /> Dice Pool - 2 Gnosis + 3 Space + 4 Mudra - 2 Sympathy -12 Potency +5 Ritual Interval.= Chance die - Willpower for +3 and Rote Exceptional Luck beyond that.<br /> <br /> Sure, the spirigam can use its Rank of 5 as a dice pool in a clash of wills vs a dice pool of 3 Space + 2 Gnosis + 4 Indefinite + 1 Adv Potency if it has a Gauntlet-crossing manifestation and that counts as &quot;the ability to step from one world to another&quot; (I'd rule it does). BUT that requires at least the Resonant condition in the Fallen World (1E + Clash of Wills for Reaching) and 3 Essence per attempt for Gauntlet Breach. A spirit will have 50 essence Max and an idigam will have 100. That's a LOT of Clashes and a LOT of Essence spent before it establishes the Condition and succeeds. If it runs out or doesn't have Reaching... it's SOL. Also... can an Exceptional Luck boon apply to Clashes of Wills?<br /> <br /> So an entry-level mage can either permaban or seriously inconvenience an inconceivable threat by werewolf standards, without breaking a sweat. This is just one example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","user":"bonerstorm","date":". 02-08-2017, 08:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T07:00:35-08:00","id":1045732,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11153\" data-vbnamecard=\"11153\">bonerstorm</a> You miscalculated Indefinite Duration, it also requires a -10 dice penalty. Advanced Potency doesn't help overcome Withstand and every point of Potency costs -2 dice (You might start off with a boost to that if Potency is the Primary Factor). Conditional Duration like that would give 1 free level of Duration at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T07:10:36-08:00","id":1045735,"title":"","content":"Plus, there's that whole pesky business of getting an sympathetic connection to the target to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T07:58:42-08:00","id":1045756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1045735#post1045735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, there's that whole pesky business of getting an sympathetic connection to the target to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, all you have to do is get one spell off on the target, or borrow a thread from someone (or something) that has. Or potentially vice versa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T08:16:53-08:00","id":1045768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1045732#post1045732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11153\" data-vbnamecard=\"11153\">bonerstorm</a> You miscalculated Indefinite Duration, it also requires a -10 dice penalty. Advanced Potency doesn't help overcome Withstand and every point of Potency costs -2 dice (You might start off with a boost to that if Potency is the Primary Factor). Conditional Duration like that would give 1 free level of Duration at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did miscalculate Advanced duration by 1 level... It's primary so the base is One week, two levels from Conditional bring it up to One Year. That's just a discrepancy of -2 to the casting roll which could be accounted for by, say, +1 to Mudra bonus and -1 penalty representational rather than symbolic yantra... or just by Material sympathy for zero penalty. I did factor in -12 for +6 potency for a total of 7, just enough to exceed Withstand by 1. Advanced Potency is for the increased dispel hassle as well as +1 to Clash of Will rolls.<br /> <br /> I'm also sure there's another Conditional Duration that would work fine, like &quot;Until this clay/glass seal is broken.&quot; In an infinite span of time, that seal WILL break. Plausibly pretty soon, depending on how clumsy the clan of thankful werewolves you gave it to are. That's THEIR problem, though.<br /> <br /> As for getting a sympathetic connection? That's what Borrow Threads is for. Find the spirit's mortal enemy and borrow/copy THEIR sympathetic connection. Or find a sample of their goo etc for a Strong connection AND a material sympathy yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T09:08:54-08:00","id":1045807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bonerstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1045689#post1045689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Draws a picture of mean old mister spirit as a -2 sympathy Yantra</div> </div> </div> </div>Sympathetic Yantras don't work by applying penalties and symbolic sympathy is going to be kind of hard to get for something as weird as an idigam to begin with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Base Potency 1 Duration 3 turns. </div> </div> </div>Gonna go out on a limb here and suppose you're talking about a rote form of Ban, which you never actually specify. Assuming my guess is correct, there's a problem with this hypothetical already.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1 Free Reach for Sensory range<br /> 1 Free Reach for Advanced Potency<br /> 1 Free Reach for Advanced Duration<br /> 1 Mana Reach for Indefinite Duration<br /> 1 mana for Sympathetic Range (+1 withstand for not knowing its probably well-known sympathetic name.. but Withstand is 4 for a weak connection anyway: Withstand 6 total)<br /> Conditional duration of &quot;Until the heat death of the sun&quot; or &quot;Until 1000 years passes&quot; or &quot;until the Earth is struck by an asteroid&quot; or another infrequent condition that will eventually happen for 2 levels of Duration. </div> </div> </div>1 Reach for Advanced Scale unless you're confident Mean Old Mister Spirit is only Size 5 and staying within a place definable by human wingspan.<br /> <br /> You're already at five Reach out of the three you get for free \u2014 possibly six, if you have literally any other spells active besides the Borrow Threads you're using to make this at all possible unless you want to make a bigger contrivance of this and say that this Spirit 0 mage has a Sanctum in the Shadow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's assume they cast in the Shadow to avoid Gauntlet Withstand (I'd rule it applies if the spell crossed it)<br /> <br /> Dice Pool - 2 Gnosis + 3 Space + 4 Mudra - 2 Sympathy -12 Potency +5 Ritual Interval.= Chance die - Willpower for +3 and Rote Exceptional Luck beyond that. </div> </div> </div>+5 Ritual Interval for a Gnosis 2 mage means eighteen solid hours of spellcasting.<br /> <br /> In the Shadow.<br /> <br /> With no dots in Spirit to either get them there or ward off the locals.<br /> <br /> When you're from nearby enough to hear werewolves complaining about this specific Shadow-corrupting servitor-making monster.<br /> <br /> Yeah, fuck that noise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So an entry-level mage can either permaban or seriously inconvenience an inconceivable threat by werewolf standards, without breaking a sweat. This is just one example. </div> </div> </div>One example which requires you to treat a spell that affects an area as a spell that affects an individual.<br /> <br /> Nope. You want to use intermediate spellcraft to sympathetically choke off one of the Moon-Banished from interaction with the outside world, you need to know if and where the big fella sleeps well enough to have a connection to it and a decent model of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Remedied miscount. 02-08-2017, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T11:30:00-08:00","id":1045879,"title":"","content":"Hey <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>,<br /> <br /> As always glad to see your posts as I often find them enlightening. I see your spell analysis and I thought I would also poke some glaring holes in this spell that seems to not be considered yet by anyone either.<br /> <br /> Hey <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11153\" data-vbnamecard=\"11153\">bonerstorm</a>,<br /> So, I am going to assume this spell casting is related to the Spell Ban, which is a 3rd Dot Practice under the Space Arcanum.<br /> <br /> Ok, so let's assume you have this spell as a Rote, which happens to grant 3 Free Reach since having a Rote grants you Master status when casting the spell.<br /> <br /> Let's say to stay within the safety zone of casting this spell without Paradox you can perform the following reaches free:<br /> 1 Free Reach for Sensory Range<br /> 1 Free Reach for Advanced Potency<br /> 1 Free Reach for Advanced Duration<br /> <br /> This would mean you have to be able to see the creature to cast this spell safely, but since our Mage is a Mastigos and has Space 3 they also have the attainment of Sympathetic Range, which adds an additional point of Mana from my understanding and requires some sympathetic connection to the target plus a yantra. Idigam are constantly changing shape, but if they have solidified into a standard shape which I think is required for Rank 5 then maybe you can get a drawing for a Representational Yantra which provides no bonus or penalty to spell casting roll.<br /> <br /> Ok, so that gives you a standard duration of 1 Month without any modifications. You then add Fate 2 for the Conditional Duration, which does up the duration by 1 point, so this puts you at 1 Year total and capping you out on Advanced Duration if not using a Reach plus Mana and taking a -10 penalty for Indefinite.<br /> <br /> The Mage I assume has no Spirit since they are a Mastigos and have Fate 2, which kind of seals the deal leaving Mind 1 as the only available option, so getting to the Shadow Realm is your first obstacle, which maybe you know a Thyrsus.<br /> <br /> So, you get into the Shadow and now need to cast a spell for 15 hours as mentioned by Satchel without anything harming you or disrupting your ritual to gain the +5 Bonus to your spell casting die pool.<br /> <br /> So, you are already at 1 Thyrsus Mage and 1 Mastigos Mage, this is now becoming a group project. You also mentioned Superlative Luck, which requires an Acanthus or someone that has Fate 3 and knows the Rote, so now it is three Mages. But also note the following:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> +2 Reach: The subject\u2019s player may apply the spell\u2019s effects to ritual spellcasting rolls, which doubles the Gnosis-derived casting time of those spells. </div> </div> </div>So your spell now takes 30 Hours to cast instead of 15. This will require a Stamina Roll just to stay up in my opinion since you are going well over 24 Hours just to attempt casting this spell and I am sure it is a taxing thing to begin with and you keep it up for that long is got to take a toll.<br /> <br /> Next, as mentioned by Satchel, this creature is probably going to be huge so you are going to need to accommodate for a space large enough to capture it. So, you need to bump it to let's say the size of a small warehouse. This requires a Reach to improve the Scale to Advanced Scale and requires a -2 penalty for the Size. Let's say you spend a point of mana to negate the Paradox to reduce this to a chance die.<br /> <br /> Know, let's determine the Potency required for this spell in order to land the effect, it is base 1 since Duration is the Primary Factor leaving you with at least a required 8 Potency.<br /> 1 (Sympathetic Range w/ Strong Sympathy) + 1 (No True Name) + 5 (Rank) = 7<br /> Your casting die pool is the following: 2 (Gnosis) + 3 (Space) + 5 (Ritual Casting) - 14 (Potency) + 4 (Rote Mudra) + 3 (Willpower) - 2 Size = 1 die w/ Superlative Luck (rote quality).<br /> <br /> You might get that spell off... might, but let's assume you don't die in the Shadow and manage to get 1 success with at most 2 die rolls.<br /> <br /> The creature is trapped behind your Ban, which it does not need to Breathe but probably needs Essence to survive. It rolls its attempts on Clash of Wills which for an Idigam is probably equivalent to the following if I recall correctly: 5 (Rank) + 5 (Influence) + 3 (Willpower) = 13.<br /> <br /> The Mage's Clash of Wills is the following: 2 (Gnosis) + 3 (Space) + 2 (Willpower) + 1 (Advanced Potency) + 4 (Year Duration) = 12 Die.<br /> <br /> Now, a Mage probably has max starting out somewhere around 7 Willpower vs. Idigam which will have 10. I think the Idigam is going to win. That is assuming the Idigam does not have a Mage Ally willing to help out.<br /> <br /> You also needed a small cabal to perform this feat. Granted a more powerful Mage would be able to instantly trap the creature with much higher chance of success, which I do find interesting. This of course is assuming the Spirit of Rank 5 does not have other protections in place, which I honestly think they would.<br /> <br /> Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Not sure how this turned into a Magic vs. Creatures in general topic. *shrugs*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T12:57:48-08:00","id":1045925,"title":"","content":"Lol pretty hostile.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1045807#post1045807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sympathetic Yantras don't work by applying penalties and representational sympathy is going to be kind of hard to get for something as weird as an idigam to begin with.<br /> <br /> Gonna go out on a limb here and suppose you're talking about a rote form of Ban, which you never actually specify. Assuming my guess is correct, there's a problem with this hypothetical already.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right! sympathy Yantras are EVEN BETTER. I think pre-errata symbolic sympathy was -2 to the casting roll (hence my math error). Now it's a flat zero when using Sympathetic Range... so it's even easier to cast than I thought!<br /> &quot;Material sympathy gives a 2-die bonus to the spellcasting pool, while representational sympathy adds +1 die. Symbolic sympathy is not close enough to the subject to give a bonus. A mage must use a sympathetic Yantra in order to cast a spell using the Sympathetic Range or Temporal Sympathy Attainments; it does not give any bonus dice when doing so.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1045807#post1045807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 Reach for Advanced Scale unless you're confident Mean Old Mister Spirit is only Size 5 and staying within a place definable by human wingspan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Touche. That said, I'm sure there are plenty of Rank 5 ephemerals with 5 size (given that Rank is a suggested Size guideline for spirits). Advanced scale and -2 is enough to go up to size 10 (which I can pay for with the 2 dice I saved when you pointed out how sympathy .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1045807#post1045807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're already at six Reach out of the three you get for free \u2014 possibly seven, if you have literally any other spells active besides the Borrow Threads you're using to make this at all possible unless you want to make a bigger contrivance of this and say that this Spirit 0 mage has a Sanctum in the Shadow.<br /> <br /> +5 Ritual Interval for a Gnosis 2 mage means eighteen solid hours of spellcasting.<br /> <br /> In the Shadow.<br /> <br /> With no dots in Spirit to either get them there or ward off the locals.<br /> <br /> When you're from nearby enough to hear werewolves complaining about this specific Shadow-corrupting servitor-making monster.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Let's say the mage has a bunch of werewolf friends who'll help in exchange for nerfing the thing that hates them and wants to eat them. They don't know a single spirit with Shadow Gateway amenable to giving the guy a lift? Aren't there wolfy powers in 2E for bringing someone across the Gauntlet? A full pack can't protect a mage in the Shadow?<br /> <br /> As for Reach... mana's a renewable resource. Even at maximum reach this spell isn't going to cost more than a few days worth of pattern scouring. And 18 hours casting? Yeah... drink a couple red bulls and punch Cthulhu in the face! Fair trade.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1045807#post1045807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One example which requires you to treat a spell that affects an area as a spell that affects an individual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha if Ban targets an AREA rather than an individual then it isn't Withstood when used offensively (which is a semi-reasonable RAW interpretation)... so it's even EASIER to nerf the Dragon. You can leave it as Potency 1 and have 12 dice worth of spell factors to play with. The mage can go out to a farm with low Gauntlet Strength and do the ritual THERE. Scrying isn't withstood either, so you can cast Ban as &quot;viewing remotely&quot; without even bothering with Sympathetic Range Withstand.<br /> <br /> So literally your explanation for why the spell doesn't work is actually an argument for why it's even easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T13:11:11-08:00","id":1045937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bonerstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1045925#post1045925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say the mage has a bunch of werewolf friends who'll help in exchange for nerfing the thing that hates them and wants to eat them. They don't know a single spirit with Shadow Gateway amenable to giving the guy a lift? Aren't there wolfy powers in 2E for bringing someone across the Gauntlet? A full pack can't protect a mage in the Shadow?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;A full pack protects a mage from casting for nearly a day in another dimension to help seal off the root of a territory-spanning threat&quot; is not the kind of casual application you seem to think it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Haha if Ban targets an AREA rather than an individual then it isn't Withstood when used offensively (which is a semi-reasonable RAW interpretation)... so it's even EASIER to nerf the Dragon. </div> </div> </div>Sympathy applies a Withstand rating and if you target the wrong area you've wasted eighteen hours turning a completely unrelated area's connections to the rest of the Shadow inside-out.<br /> <br /> Also you have no means of guaranteeing that the idigam is in one world or another at any given point without further complicating the scenario. Like, yes, if you coordinate with the resources of a cult of dimension-hopping shapeshifters and their spirit-blooded brethren you can corner a god with two spells. Getting that far is another matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can leave it as Potency 1 and have 12 dice worth of spell factors to play with. </div> </div> </div>If you've got the guts to stand right in front of a minor god for hours at a time and it lacks the wherewithal to leave or strike you down, sure. Otherwise you get to deal with the problems of finding the place and getting it to stay there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The mage can go out to a farm with low Gauntlet Strength and do the ritual THERE. Scrying isn't withstood either, so you can cast Ban as &quot;viewing remotely&quot; without even bothering with Sympathetic Range Withstand. </div> </div> </div>Scrying doesn't have an innate Withstand rating because its most useful effect engages with Sympathetic Range (and Gauntlet Withstand if you're not on the same side as the target). Using a Yantra corresponding to a discrete target tends to provide a view too narrow to actually tell you anything about where it is and subsequently Ban it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T13:22:38-08:00","id":1045948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1045879#post1045879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11153\" data-vbnamecard=\"11153\">bonerstorm</a>,<br /> So, I am going to assume this spell casting is related to the Spell Ban, which is a 3rd Dot Practice under the Space Arcanum.<br /> <br /> Ok, so let's assume you have this spell as a Rote, which happens to grant 3 Free Reach since having a Rote grants you Master status when casting the spell.<br /> <br /> Let's say to stay within the safety zone of casting this spell without Paradox you can perform the following reaches free:<br /> 1 Free Reach for Sensory Range<br /> 1 Free Reach for Advanced Potency<br /> 1 Free Reach for Advanced Duration<br /> <br /> This would mean you have to be able to see the creature to cast this spell safely, but since our Mage is a Mastigos and has Space 3 they also have the attainment of Sympathetic Range, which adds an additional point of Mana from my understanding and requires some sympathetic connection to the target plus a yantra. Idigam are constantly changing shape, but if they have solidified into a standard shape which I think is required for Rank 5 then maybe you can get a drawing for a Representational Yantra which provides no bonus or penalty to spell casting roll.<br /> <br /> Ok, so that gives you a standard duration of 1 Month without any modifications. You then add Fate 2 for the Conditional Duration, which does up the duration by 1 point, so this puts you at 1 Year total and capping you out on Advanced Duration if not using a Reach plus Mana and taking a -10 penalty for Indefinite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Conditional duration can up levels by up to 3. I think &quot;Until this clay/glass/whatever seal is broken&quot; is pretty reasonable for 2 levels. I was originally and you are now wrong with the duration math: 3 levels from Primary Factor puts base at 1 week. With 2 from Conditional, it still requires another -2 to bring it up to Indefinite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1045879#post1045879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mage I assume has no Spirit since they are a Mastigos and have Fate 2, which kind of seals the deal leaving Mind 1 as the only available option, so getting to the Shadow Realm is your first obstacle, which maybe you know a Thyrsus.<br /> <br /> So, you get into the Shadow and now need to cast a spell for 15 hours as mentioned by Satchel without anything harming you or disrupting your ritual to gain the +5 Bonus to your spell casting die pool.<br /> <br /> So, you are already at 1 Thyrsus Mage and 1 Mastigos Mage, this is now becoming a group project. You also mentioned Superlative Luck, which requires an Acanthus or someone that has Fate 3 and knows the Rote, so now it is three Mages. But also note the following:<br /> <br /> <br /> So your spell now takes 30 Hours to cast instead of 15. This will require a Stamina Roll just to stay up in my opinion since you are going well over 24 Hours just to attempt casting this spell and I am sure it is a taxing thing to begin with and you keep it up for that long is got to take a toll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exceptional Luck is Fate 2, which the aforementioned mage already has and does not double spellcasting times.<br /> <br /> Also there are plenty of ways to cross the Gauntlet without another mage. If we're talking about an idigam, there are likely several packs who would LOVE to work with a mage to bind it. We'll also see below how Satchel convinced me we don't even NEED to go into the Shadow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1045879#post1045879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next, as mentioned by Satchel, this creature is probably going to be huge so you are going to need to accommodate for a space large enough to capture it. So, you need to bump it to let's say the size of a small warehouse. This requires a Reach to improve the Scale to Advanced Scale and requires a -2 penalty for the Size. Let's say you spend a point of mana to negate the Paradox to reduce this to a chance die.<br /> <br /> Know, let's determine the Potency required for this spell in order to land the effect, it is base 1 since Duration is the Primary Factor leaving you with at least a required 8 Potency.<br /> 1 (Sympathetic Range w/ Strong Sympathy) + 1 (No True Name) + 5 (Rank) = 7<br /> Your casting die pool is the following: 2 (Gnosis) + 3 (Space) + 5 (Ritual Casting) - 14 (Potency) + 4 (Rote Mudra) + 3 (Willpower) - 2 Size = 1 die w/ Superlative Luck (rote quality).<br /> <br /> You might get that spell off... might, but let's assume you don't die in the Shadow and manage to get 1 success with at most 2 die rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK that's another -2. Sure you spend mana.. whoop de doo. You're punching Cthulhu. Who cares if it isn't free?<br /> <br /> So the all-wise and all-knowing and more-than-a-little-condescending Satchel noted that Ban affects an area, not an individual, so it can't be Withstood. Makes our job a LOT easier!<br /> <br /> 2 Gnosis + 3 Space + 5 Ritual Casting -2 Duration -10 Potency -2 Scale +4 Rote Mudra = Chance Die + Willpower + Exceptional Luck (flat bonus, not rote). Why did I add in 5 potency there when I didn't need ANY? Because that's the maximum natural Withstand value of the Gauntlet... so you can cast it in the comfort of your own sanctum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1045879#post1045879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The creature is trapped behind your Ban, which it does not need to Breathe but probably needs Essence to survive. It rolls its attempts on Clash of Wills which for an Idigam is probably equivalent to the following if I recall correctly: 5 (Rank) + 5 (Influence) + 3 (Willpower) = 13.<br /> <br /> The Mage's Clash of Wills is the following: 2 (Gnosis) + 3 (Space) + 2 (Willpower) + 1 (Advanced Potency) + 4 (Year Duration) = 12 Die.<br /> <br /> Now, a Mage probably has max starting out somewhere around 7 Willpower vs. Idigam which will have 10. I think the Idigam is going to win. That is assuming the Idigam does not have a Mage Ally willing to help out.<br /> <br /> You also needed a small cabal to perform this feat. Granted a more powerful Mage would be able to instantly trap the creature with much higher chance of success, which I do find interesting. This of course is assuming the Spirit of Rank 5 does not have other protections in place, which I honestly think they would.<br /> <br /> Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Not sure how this turned into a Magic vs. Creatures in general topic. *shrugs*</div> </div> </div> </div>Ephemerals Clash with only Rank, as I and another pointed out above. AND the spirigam needs to use Reaching then influence to apply Resonance for Gauntlet Breach... so they have to win TWO COW's and spend Essence with each attempt. The mage may not win... but they'll REALLY ruin this thing's day.<br /> <br /> And... an Idigam with a mage ally? Most listed only have basic minions because they're spiritual Hitlers. They'd probably spend all their time trying to figure out what's going on, then try to break the seal. And, nope, idigams and spirits don't have Signs &amp; Wards. Not a thing. If you wanna make those numina, they're your houserules.<br /> <br /> Eh? I was just trying to point out that Mage can be a little unbalanced (e.g. effortlessly binding minor gods for low-level chars), so I houserule things to even them out. I'm surprised anyone would feel much differently, let alone so strongly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","user":"bonerstorm","date":". 02-08-2017, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T13:34:27-08:00","id":1045960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1045937#post1045937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;A full pack protects a mage from casting for nearly a day in another dimension to help seal off the root of a territory-spanning threat&quot; is not the kind of casual application you seem to think it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you proved to me that going into the Gauntlet isn't even necessary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1045937#post1045937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sympathy applies a Withstand rating and if you target the wrong area you've wasted eighteen hours turning a completely unrelated area's connections to the rest of the Shadow inside-out.<br /> <br /> Also you have no means of guaranteeing that the idigam is in one world or another at any given point without further complicating the scenario. Like, yes, if you coordinate with the resources of a cult of dimension-hopping shapeshifters and their spirit-blooded brethren you can corner a god with two spells. Getting that far is another matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once you're scrying, Sympathy for Ban is irrelevant. You're casting while viewing remotely, which is just another reach and isn't Withstood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1045937#post1045937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scrying doesn't have an innate Withstand rating because its most useful effect engages with Sympathetic Range (and Gauntlet Withstand if you're not on the same side as the target). Using a Yantra corresponding to a discrete target tends to provide a view too narrow to actually tell you anything about where it is and subsequently Ban it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there anything in the rules that says you can't scale a scrying window? The rules are squishy:<br /> &quot;to a person or object tends to show a \u201cclose up\u201d of the subject<br /> \u2014 the window will follow the subject if it moves, but the mage<br /> may not be able to make out details of where the subject is or<br /> who else might be present.&quot;<br /> <br /> Even if you can't, where does it say that I can't cast a Ban which encompasses everything I DO see (which is presumably enough to show the contours of their body)? The rules are unclear and mostly line up to &quot;you MAY not be able to use this spell to figure out where someone is or who someone's with.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T13:43:22-08:00","id":1045967,"title":"","content":"Hell... without ANY of this wacky Sympathetic Range stuff, the same mage can cast the same spell in 2 turns flat for 4 Mana within Sensory range:<br /> 2 Gnosis + 3 Space + 4 Mudra +2 Mantra - 2 Duration - 2 Scale - 2 Potency = 5 Dice. You can subtract -4 to not even NEED to use Conditional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T13:49:08-08:00","id":1045974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bonerstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1045967#post1045967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell... without ANY of this wacky Sympathetic Range stuff, the same mage can cast the same spell in 2 turns flat for 4 Mana within Sensory range:<br /> 2 Gnosis + 3 Space + 4 Mudra +2 Mantra - 2 Duration - 2 Scale - 2 Potency = 5 Dice. You can subtract -4 to not even NEED to use Conditional.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So? Also you forgot about adding willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T14:04:52-08:00","id":1045987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bonerstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1045960#post1045960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once you're scrying, Sympathy for Ban is irrelevant. You're casting while viewing remotely, which is just another reach and isn't Withstood.</div> </div> </div> </div>And getting Scrying to work outside sensory range requires overcoming Sympathetic Withstand. Scrying into the Shadow from the material world or vice versa adds Spirit to the requirements and Gauntlet Withstand as a concern besides, on top of layering yet another spell onto your spell control.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there anything in the rules that says you can't scale a scrying window? The rules are squishy<br /> [\u2026]<br /> Even if you can't, where does it say that I can't cast a Ban which encompasses everything I DO see (which is presumably enough to show the contours of their body)? The rules are unclear and mostly line up to &quot;you MAY not be able to use this spell to figure out where someone is or who someone's with.&quot; </div> </div> </div>You're basing your argument here on doesn't-say, which is generally the point at which an argument ceases to be compelling.<br /> <br /> The narrative role of Scrying based on individual sympathy is targeting individuals for personal interaction and the narrative role of Ban is to seal off a defined space. If you make use of <i>yet another</i> spell (e.g. The Outward and Inward Eye with its +2 Reach effect) or some other contrivance (like sending a Familiar to infiltrate the place) to piece together what its location is like from the limited view afforded by personal Scrying, you might be able to get the kind of picture needed to incorporate the symbolism of a place into your Imago, but by that point you're looking at three or four different spells sustained on the bus space of Gnosis 2 spell control just to look at the thing and target the area around it \u2014 and adding Exceptional Luck only further complicates the matter, particularly since the &quot;add 2 Reach to apply a boon to spellcasting rolls&quot; is specifically listed under the &quot;add 9-Again&quot; subtype.<br /> <br /> So yes, <i>if</i> you have a starting character with three specific rotes, the assistance of a pack of werewolves, the time and resources to blow on spending half your Mana pool on reducing Paradox risk, and the good fortune to have a target that will stay still for long enough that you can ward a specific location over the course of nearly a full day of casting from a different location while almost certainly lacking the ability to account for the chance that it isn't there, you can <i>theoretically</i> block off a minor god from interaction with the wider world in a manner that is blindingly obvious to anyone who looks at the Ban.<br /> <br /> This is not a trivial application of arcane might, to say nothing of the problems that can still arise from any servants the creature made still running around, the impact of cutting off a part of the world from the rest of the world, the possibility that the idigam is in Twilight in proximity to Sleepers, the chance that another mage stumbles across your unshielded spell and gets curious, or you just plain fail to contain the Paradox and wind up losing a vital spell factor from the mix or attracting Abyssal phenomena to the area through your Nimbus.<br /> <br /> To treat these as non-issues is disingenuous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-08-2017, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T14:10:05-08:00","id":1045990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1045987#post1045987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And getting Scrying to work outside sensory range requires overcoming Sympathetic Withstand. Scrying into the Shadow from the material world or vice versa <b>adds Spirit to the requirements </b>and Gauntlet Withstand as a concern besides, on top of layering yet another spell onto your spell control.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't. A place is a place just like mind is a mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T14:16:20-08:00","id":1045992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1045990#post1045990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't. A place is a place just like mind is a mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;A mind is a mind&quot; does not scan to the problems of crossing the Gauntlet. Your views on conjunctional requirements do not circumvent the established precedent of Psychic Projection, The Outward and Inward Eye, Teleportation, and the unique purviews of the Spirit Arcanum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T14:38:17-08:00","id":1046004,"title":"","content":"Gauntlet adds a withstand and thats it. Psychic Projection adds Spirit to cross it without Sympathy, of course it needs some means to target a Gauntlet. The same goes to Teleportation, imo. <br /> Outward and Inward Eye is weird - if you can't perceive whats on the other side of Iris you need arcanum to open it, thats true, but if you can see it with your mundane eyes? You don't need it.<br /> If you see whats on the other side of the Gauntlet you don't need Spirit to cast a remote spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T14:45:34-08:00","id":1046009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1046004#post1046004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you see whats on the other side of the Gauntlet you don't need Spirit to cast a remote spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm saying that you <i>can't</i> open a window through the Gauntlet (which is what Scrying into Shadow does) without Spirit. A Familiar might provide the necessary channel to circumvent the Gauntlet, but an ephemeral being with Connected Sympathy to you whose senses you can freely share is not engaging with spellcasting in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T15:26:22-08:00","id":1046028,"title":"","content":"Sure you can. It might be more difficult to gain a sympathetic connection to stuff in the Shadow, but that doesn't make Spirit a requirement. Once you've managed to gain a sympathetic connection it's just a matter of Withstand. There's no &quot;Add Spirit X: You can now cast from across the Gauntlet&quot;. The Gauntlet just adds a Withstand rating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T15:33:07-08:00","id":1046031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1046009#post1046009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'm saying that you <i>can't</i> open a window through the Gauntlet (which is what Scrying into Shadow does) without Spirit. A Familiar might provide the necessary channel to circumvent the Gauntlet, but an ephemeral being with Connected Sympathy to you whose senses you can freely share is not engaging with spellcasting in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point! I haven't seen any general rules stating that Sympathetic Range spells crossing the Gauntlet etc. require Spirit Arcanum... but that's not an unreasonable ruling to make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T15:44:31-08:00","id":1046034,"title":"","content":"But it would definitely be a house rule. I don't think that's the kind of thing the devs just forgot to include. I find it more likely they didn't think it was a necessary limitation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T15:46:58-08:00","id":1046036,"title":"","content":"The problem would be to perceive the Shadow since its made of ephemera and essence so you'll need at least Spirit 1 and another spell. But Sympathy has no boundaries and Gauntlet can't stop it. You affect the target directly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T15:53:28-08:00","id":1046038,"title":"","content":"You can see the Shadow just fine. The reason ephemera is normally invisible in the material world is because it's in Twilight. Ephemera in the Shadow is just as physically present as any material objects in the material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T16:00:42-08:00","id":1046040,"title":"","content":"So from my understanding this is how this spell would need to work at your Sanctum:<br /> You need Spirit 1, Space 3, Gnosis 2, Ban Rote, and Scry Rote.<br /> Ban is a 3 dot Space Spell and is a Rote, so you have 3 Free Reach to play with.<br /> Scry is a 2 Dot Space Spell and is a Rote, so you have 4 Reach to play with.<br /> Exceptional Luck is on you as a Spell.<br /> <br /> That is 3 Spells, which means you are going to suffer 1 Reach worth of Paradox due to spell control issues.<br /> <br /> You also need to defeat Gauntlet Strength as the following indicates:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> pg. 179 MtAw2E: Any spell cast on a subject on the other side of the Gauntlet or on the Gauntlet itself is Withstood by the Gauntlet Strength. </div> </div> </div>Your target is across the Gauntlet so you need to defeat the strength at the location. (Typically 3/4) Let's say Strength of 4.<br /> You would need to be able to Scry on the target, which I believe just requires a Sympathetic Connection and Yantra along with Sympathetic Range. (1 Reach for Sensory Range &amp; 1 Mana to Cast Sympathetically)<br /> The Scrying Spell requires a Potency of 8. (4 Gauntlet Strength + 1 Don't Know True Name + 1 for Strong Sympathetic Connection +1 for Additional Withstand).<br /> <br /> Your die pool is the following for this: 2 (Gnosis) + 3 (Space) + 4 (Rote Mudra) -14 (Potency) + 5 (Ritual Casting) + 3 (Willpower) = 3 Die.<br /> <br /> But let's say you lived in the wilderness (for some reason) and thus only need a Potency of 6. (2 Gauntlet Strength + 1 Don't Know True Name + 1 for Strong Sympathetic Connection +1 for Additional Withstand).<br /> <br /> Your die pool is now the following for this: 2 (Gnosis) + 3 (Space) + 4 (Rote Mudra) -10 (Potency) + 3 (Willpower) + 2 (Ritual Casting) = 4 Die. You may be a little tired, but this is doable.<br /> <br /> Next, once you can see the area where your target is located, you need to cast the Ban on that area, which again requires a Potency of at least 3 in order to take effect since it just needs to beat the Gauntlet Strength.<br /> You need 1 Reach to Cast with Advanced Duration.<br /> You need 1 Reach to Cast within Sensory Range.<br /> You need 1 Reach to Cast while viewing Remotely.<br /> You need 1 Reach to for Advanced Scale.<br /> You use 1 Mana for the Conditional Duration Factor of +2 granting a Duration of 1 Year.<br /> You use 1 Mana to reduce the Paradox Roll to 1 Die.<br /> Total 4 Reach and 2 Mana<br /> <br /> Your die pool for Ban is the following now: 2 (Gnosis) + 3 (Space) + 4 (Rote Mudra) - 4 (Potency) - 2 (Size) = 3 Die w/ Exceptional Luck.<br /> <br /> This will effectively Ban the Rank 5 Creature for sometime with its Clash of Wills equivalent to 5 vs.10.<br /> <br /> For all intents and purposes, mechanically that Idigam is trapped assuming it is unable to have an ally aid the creature.<br /> <br /> You can't make the spell indefinite since it requires the following without risking some serious paradox plus you need higher gnosis:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Doing so can increase the Duration of a spell, although the mage must still spend Mana and a Reach if Duration becomes indefinite </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":". 02-08-2017, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T16:05:45-08:00","id":1046042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1046038#post1046038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can see the Shadow just fine. The reason ephemera is normally invisible in the material world is because it's in Twilight. Ephemera in the Shadow is just as physically present as any material objects in the material.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a matter of interpretation of course but I see it differently. &quot;Material&quot; is just another Twilight frequency. Our world contains many of those Twilights but Shadow has only one, Spirit related one. If you cross the Gauntlet you are shifted into this new Twilight because you have no other choice. <br /> But with scrying you don't travel anywhere and don't change Twilights. And when you are on different wavelengths you can't see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 02-08-2017, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T16:08:21-08:00","id":1046044,"title":"","content":"Teleportation is a special case, probably because you're &quot;breaching&quot; two worlds rather than making the effect of a spell take place in one. It's not a general rule or it wouldn't be written in a single specific spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T16:19:14-08:00","id":1046047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1046042#post1046042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a matter of interpretation of course but I see it differently. &quot;Material&quot; is just another Twilight frequency. Our world contains many of those Twilights but Shadow has only one, Spirit related one. If you cross the Gauntlet you are shifted into this new Twilight because you have no other choice.<br /> But with scrying you don't travel anywhere and don't change Twilight's. And when you are on different wavelength's you can't see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an interesting interpretation, but it's not how it works in the default setting. The book defines Twilight as a state of being that is not material. I.e. the material is not Twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T16:25:43-08:00","id":1046053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1046044#post1046044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Teleportation is a special case, probably because you're &quot;breaching&quot; two worlds rather than making the effect of a spell take place in one. It's not a general rule or it wouldn't be written in a single specific spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. The sad part is the Rank 5 Spirit has such a low Clash of Wills roll, I thought it was Rank + Influence, but only if appropriate. That is quite silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T16:26:15-08:00","id":1046054,"title":"","content":"Double post","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 02-08-2017, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T16:28:50-08:00","id":1046057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1046047#post1046047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's an interesting interpretation, but it's not how it works in the default setting. The book defines Twilight as a state of being that is not material. I.e. the material is not Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's no RAW but it explains nicely why spirits end up in Spirit Twilight in our world but we don't land in a Human Twilight after crossing the Gauntlet. <br /> You have a different explanation why that happens? I'm just curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T16:36:57-08:00","id":1046060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1046038#post1046038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can see the Shadow just fine. The reason ephemera is normally invisible in the material world is because it's in Twilight. Ephemera in the Shadow is just as physically present as any material objects in the material.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ephemera is visible in the Shadow because <i>everything in the Shadow is spiritual ephemera</i>. If you can't even see spiritual ephemera in Twilight, why should Scrying translate an entire world made of the stuff into a comprehensible visual on its own?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T16:44:22-08:00","id":1046065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ephemera is visible in the Shadow because <i>everything in the Shadow is spiritual ephemera</i>. If you can't even see spiritual ephemera in Twilight, why should Scrying translate an entire world made of the stuff into a comprehensible visual on its own? </div> </div> </div>This is also a good point. It makes sense you would need at least Spirit 1 to be able to translate what you are seeing. Just like you need Death 1 to see Ghosts. So, perhaps you need at least Spirit 1. That aside I feel Ban got a huge upgrade in 2E and it seems Spirits lost the ability to Clash making them pretty feeble against even a starting a Mage. You could technically have made a Space 3, Mind 2, and Spirit 1 Mage to accomplish the same thing. Technically you would not need Fate 2 for the Exceptional Luck since you have a sizable die pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":". 02-08-2017, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T16:50:49-08:00","id":1046067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1046065#post1046065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is also a good point. It makes sense you would need at least Spirit 1 to be able to translate what you are seeing. Just like you need Death 1 to see Ghosts. So, perhaps you need at least Spirit 1. That aside I feel Ban got a huge upgrade in 2E and it seems Spirits lost the ability to Clash making them pretty feeble against even a starting a Mage. You could technically have made a Space 3, Fate 2, and Spirit 1 Mage to accomplish the same thing. Technically you would not need Fate 2 for the Exceptional Luck since you have a sizable die pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I don't understand why you would need scrying and perceiving Shadow in a first place. Just Ban it up in a first spell. Cool guys don't look at explosions. <br /> The part about spirits withstand and clash bothers me, though. I'd didn't come up in my game but it feels unbalanced","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T16:59:42-08:00","id":1046073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I don't understand why you would need scrying and perceiving Shadow in a first place. Just Ban it up in a first spell. Cool guys don't look at explosions. </div> </div> </div>True, I suppose just Sympathetically Banning the creature would also work. Less spells to control plus with Scrying you can take the backlash of the creature attacking you with some Numina or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T18:20:31-08:00","id":1046101,"title":"","content":"I see they're confusing spirits for idigam. Nevermind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-08-2017, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T18:41:39-08:00","id":1046109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1046060#post1046060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ephemera is visible in the Shadow because <i>everything in the Shadow is spiritual ephemera</i>. If you can't even see spiritual ephemera in Twilight, why should Scrying translate an entire world made of the stuff into a comprehensible visual on its own?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying I'm necessarily right now, but I suggest that the reason ephemera is invisible in the material world is because it's in Twilight, not because that quality is inherent in ephemera. In such a case it would make perfect sense that the Shadow and the Underworld (and the Gauntlet) are visible without translation aid, because Twilight is exclusive to the material plane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T18:57:45-08:00","id":1046116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1045150#post1045150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, the problem with this list is that you CAN use Mind to mess with Demons just fine. That is the equivlency you are looking for, not Angels.<br /> <br /> And as others have said, Mind works on Angels, as long as it doesn't go against their Mission.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u200b should not be that hard to do just that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T19:02:06-08:00","id":1046120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1046116#post1046116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u200b should not be that hard to do just that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you think that?<br /> <br /> Angels are programmed a certain way. Trying to mind control one into going against its mission is like trying to mind control a human to flapping its wings and flying into the sun, or to stop time by using their fourth eye. It's a physical impossibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T19:32:51-08:00","id":1046131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1046120#post1046120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why do you think that?<br /> <br /> Angels are programmed a certain way. Trying to mind control one into going against its mission is like trying to mind control a human to flapping its wings and flying into the sun, or to stop time by using their fourth eye. It's a physical impossibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI don't think mind control is the right way. It's better to do something like a mind scan of surface thoughts or an indirect suggestion based on those thoughts so that a CoW shouldn't be provoked. Be the nail or scalpel not the hammer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 02-08-2017, 10:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T19:50:29-08:00","id":1046138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041571-angels-and-mind-magic?p=1046109#post1046109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying I'm necessarily right now, but I suggest that the reason ephemera is invisible in the material world is because it's in Twilight, not because that quality is inherent in ephemera.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm saying that the natural state of ephemera in the material world <i>is the state of Twilight</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lexicon, &quot;Twilight&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The state of existence of most ephemeral beings</b> (including ghosts, Goetia, and spirits)<b> when in the material world</b>. Twilight objects and beings <b>cannot be seen or touched except by magical means.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Realms Invisible, p244, &quot;The Shadow&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every location in the material realm possesses a Shadow counterpart. So do most objects, though in some cases, fallen trees and wrecked buildings still stand, maintained by the spiritual significance they possessed while they stood in the ordinary world. <b>They\u2019re made of ephemera, like everything else in the Shadow. Anyone and anything that crosses over changes into ephemeral matter,</b> and automatically changes back when it returns to the material plane. <b>Anything that began as ephemera arrives in the material world in Twilight.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Invisible Entities, p252, &quot;Denizens of Other Realms&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Collectively, Goetia, spirits, and ghosts are known as ephemeral entities, after the substance their bodies are made of when in the material world. <b>Ephemera is naturally invisible and intangible, putting the entity into Twilight unless revealed by its own powers or magic.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In such a case it would make perfect sense that the Shadow and the Underworld (and the Gauntlet) are visible without translation aid, because Twilight is exclusive to the material plane. </div> </div> </div>Adding particular varieties of Twilight to a space that lacks it is a function of that type of ephemera's governing Arcanum.<br /> <br /> The gameline has compared accessing other dimensions to simple changes of perspective on multiple occasions; a Scrying window to the Shadow opens a direct sensory connection to a world made entirely out of spiritual ephemera \u2014 if you cannot translate that conduit <i>to align with spiritual ephemera</i> then it's simply not going to get you anywhere \u2014 there's nothing to indicate that Gauntlet Withstand is ever even negotiated by spells without the Spirit Arcanum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T02:44:45-08:00","id":1046223,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> The only way for it to work would be for Shadow to have <i>only </i>Spirit Twilight. And because it's the only one available it acts <i>as </i>a &quot;Material&quot; but only for those who are already there, translated into it. <br /> <br /> So I have it like this:<br /> <b>1 dot</b> spells let you perceive phenomena and then act on them with <i>another </i>spell like e.g. Unraveling Gauntlet with Death 4 cast after Spirit 1 Unveiling Gauntlet<br /> <b>2 dot </b>requirements acts as way of incorporating Unveiling effect into other spells so you don't need to cast it separately(kind of like with increased complexity of Weaving-&gt;Patterning, you can actually achieve the with Weaving the same as with Patterning but it will tak more spells) so you could cast Rip the Gauntlet (Death 4, Spirit 2) in a single spell.<br /> <b>Sympathy</b>, if you ever gain it for Gauntlet?, can omit the Spirit arcanum altogether and just cast Death 4 Unraveling through Sympathy<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T04:05:53-08:00","id":1046240,"title":"","content":"The way people are using Twilight in this thread is so confusing. Twilight is just a fancy word for &quot;made of intangible ephemera.&quot; Its not a place, its not a dimension, its just that you're made up of something that naturally cannot be seen or experienced with the human senses.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. The Hisil is made up entirely of animistic &quot;spirit ephemera.&quot; If you want to call that &quot;Spirit Twilight,&quot; sure. But it should be noted that, yes, the Hisil is made up entirely of the same kind of essence that you can't see from reality.<br /> <br /> The reason you don't need the Spirit Arcana to see things in the Hisil when you're there yourself is that, during the process of crossing over, your body was transformed into ephemera as well. This is no different than using Ghost Gate to turn yourself into ghost-ephemera and seeing all the ghosts without Death Arcana.<br /> <br /> Should you be able to see across the Gauntlet without Spirit Arcana? My knee jerk reaction is to say &quot;no.&quot; Why? Because Mage is a game that's all about having the right tools for the right job. Its about having the right knowlege set to apply the right magical formulas. Seeing and targetting spirits without the right tools is kind of against the grain of the game, as far as I can tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-09-2017, 07:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T05:05:36-08:00","id":1046251,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2102_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2102\" data-vbnamecard=\"2102\">MCN</a> I don't think anyone is equating Twilight to a place, it's a discussion of if you need Spirit to see into the Shadow when not translated into ephemera the same as you'd need Spirit to see into Spirit-attuned Twilight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-m